cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TinyEngram in teaching or research, please cite this repository."
title: "TinyEngram: A Test-Driven Course on Conditional Memory"
abstract: "A ten-lab, test-driven course that implements DeepSeek Engram conditional memory from scratch: tokenizer compression, multi-head n-gram hashing, retrieval, context gating, short convolution, TinyLM training, sparsity allocation, host offload, and mechanistic analysis."
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-22
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/colorful-lollipop/tinyengram"
url: "https://github.com/colorful-lollipop/tinyengram"
keywords:
  - large language models
  - conditional memory
  - Engram
  - n-gram
  - mixture of experts
  - sparsity
  - PyTorch
  - education
authors:
